    {
      "slug": "the-last-tram-depot",
      "title": "The last tram depot",
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "categories": [
        "city-sounds"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "trains",
        "late-night",
        "field-recording"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/city.jpg",
      "excerpt": "At closing time the Hikawa tram depot switches its lights off one row at a time. We stayed until the last one, with the driver who parks the last car.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__play\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__play\"><a href=\"https://feeds.example.com/oto-radio/48\">Listen</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen__info\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen__info\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__no\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__no\">Episode 48</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__time\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__time\">52 min</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-wave\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wave\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__note\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__note\">Recorded on location and in Studio B. Plays in your podcast app.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The last tram of the night reaches the Hikawa depot at 00:41. After that, nobody hurries: the cars are washed, the poles are lowered with a sound like a long breath, and the lights over the tracks go off one row at a time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">In this episode</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-rundown\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-rundown\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:00</strong> <span>Cold open: the pole coming down</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:04</strong> <span>The depot after the last run, twenty minutes uncut</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:24</strong> <span>Masa Fujikawa, who has parked the last car for nineteen years</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:44</strong> <span>Letters about the sounds of your commute</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:56</strong> <span>The closing record</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>People think the last tram is the quiet one. It is the loudest. Everybody on it is talking, because they made it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Masa Fujikawa, tram driver</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Played after the show</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Masa chose “Platform Four” by the Hikawa Line Orchestra, a song he says he has never heard on a tram and never wants to.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-credits\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-credits\">Recorded by Nao Hoshino. Produced by Emi Tachibana. Mixed by Daichi Arai.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "a-record-shop-that-only-opens-when-it-rains",
      "title": "A record shop that only opens when it rains",
      "date": "2026-10-02",
      "categories": [
        "conversations"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "vinyl",
        "rain",
        "music"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/vinyl.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Yuki Sawamura opens her shop only on rainy days, because that is when people stay long enough to listen. We waited three weeks for the forecast.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__play\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__play\"><a href=\"https://feeds.example.com/oto-radio/47\">Listen</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen__info\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen__info\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__no\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__no\">Episode 47</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__time\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__time\">46 min</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-wave\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wave\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__note\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__note\">Recorded on location and in Studio B. Plays in your podcast app.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The sign on the door of Ame Records says nothing about opening hours, only an umbrella. Yuki Sawamura opens when it rains, because on dry days people browse and leave, and on wet days they stay for a whole side.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{theme}}/assets/images/vinyl.jpg\" alt=\"A turntable with its lid open beside a stack of plain black records\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The listening table at the back of the shop.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">In this episode</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-rundown\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-rundown\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:00</strong> <span>Cold open: rain on a shop awning</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:04</strong> <span>An afternoon in the shop, with the door open</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:24</strong> <span>Yuki Sawamura on why dry days are bad for records</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:44</strong> <span>Your letters about places that only open sometimes</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:56</strong> <span>The closing record</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Rain makes people honest. Nobody pretends to be in a hurry when their shoes are wet.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Yuki Sawamura, Ame Records</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Played after the show</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yuki chose a side, not a song: the whole of side B of “Low Ceiling” by Mariko Ueda and the Weather.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-credits\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-credits\">Recorded by Nao Hoshino. Produced by Emi Tachibana. Mixed by Daichi Arai.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "emi-answers-the-letters-box",
      "title": "Emi answers the letters box",
      "date": "2026-09-25",
      "categories": [
        "listener-letters"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "letters",
        "late-night"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/headphones.jpg",
      "excerpt": "No place this week: the letters box was full. Forty letters about laundromats, one about a heron, and the night bus that stops at the depot.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__play\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__play\"><a href=\"https://feeds.example.com/oto-radio/46\">Listen</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen__info\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen__info\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__no\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__no\">Episode 46</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__time\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__time\">38 min</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-wave\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wave\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__note\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__note\">Recorded on location and in Studio B. Plays in your podcast app.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every few months the letters box wins. This week Emi read for the whole hour, Nao played back the sounds you described, and Sora Kamiya, who opens every envelope, came to the microphone for the first time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">In this episode</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-rundown\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-rundown\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:00</strong> <span>Cold open: forty envelopes on a desk</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:06</strong> <span>Letters about laundromats, with the sounds you asked for</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:21</strong> <span>Chika from Setagaya and the night bus</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:38</strong> <span>Sora explains how letters are chosen</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:52</strong> <span>The closing record</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I play it on the night bus home. Last week the bus stopped outside the same tram depot you were recording in, and I heard it twice.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Chika, Setagaya</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-credits\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-credits\">Recorded and produced in Studio B by Emi Tachibana and Sora Kamiya.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "the-tuner-who-fixes-radios-by-ear",
      "title": "The tuner who fixes radios by ear",
      "date": "2026-09-18",
      "categories": [
        "conversations"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "radio",
        "interview",
        "repair"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/studio.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Goro Hanabusa has repaired radios for fifty years without an oscilloscope. He listens to the hiss until it tells him what is wrong.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__play\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__play\"><a href=\"https://feeds.example.com/oto-radio/45\">Listen</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen__info\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen__info\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__no\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__no\">Episode 45</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__time\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__time\">58 min</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-wave\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wave\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__note\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__note\">Recorded on location and in Studio B. Plays in your podcast app.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Goro Hanabusa’s workshop is two metres wide and full of radios that have not spoken in years. He switches each one on, leans in and listens to the hiss. Most of the time, he says, it tells him exactly which part has given up.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{theme}}/assets/images/studio.jpg\" alt=\"A mixing desk with rows of knobs beside a reel-to-reel tape machine\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">We brought one of his radios back to the studio and played the show through it.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">In this episode</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-rundown\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-rundown\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:00</strong> <span>Cold open: a radio warming up after thirty years</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:04</strong> <span>The workshop, with eleven radios humming at once</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:24</strong> <span>Goro Hanabusa on listening for faults</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:46</strong> <span>Letters: the radio you grew up with</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:56</strong> <span>The closing record, through a 1962 valve set</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A broken radio is never silent. It is telling you something. Most people just do not wait long enough.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Goro Hanabusa, radio repairer</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-credits\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-credits\">Recorded by Nao Hoshino. Produced by Emi Tachibana. Mixed by Daichi Arai.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "walking-the-river-at-three",
      "title": "Walking the river at three in the morning",
      "date": "2026-09-11",
      "categories": [
        "night-walks"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "river",
        "field-recording",
        "late-night"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/host1.jpg",
      "excerpt": "A night walk with no guest: Nao follows the river from the bridge to the sea wall between three and five, with two microphones and one heron.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__play\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__play\"><a href=\"https://feeds.example.com/oto-radio/44\">Listen</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"oto-listen__info\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group oto-listen__info\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__no\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__no\">Episode 44</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__time\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__time\">41 min</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-wave\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wave\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-listen__note\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-listen__note\">Recorded on location and in Studio B. Plays in your podcast app.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Night walks are the episodes with nobody to interview. Nao walks, the recorder runs, and the only voice is hers, whispering the time every fifteen minutes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">In this episode</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-rundown\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-rundown\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:00</strong> <span>Cold open: water under the bridge at 03:00</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:03</strong> <span>The walk, almost uncut</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:34</strong> <span>A heron, and a delivery van that stopped to watch it</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>00:39</strong> <span>The closing record</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"oto-credits\"} -->\n<p class=\"oto-credits\">Recorded by Nao Hoshino. Produced by Emi Tachibana.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
